<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- App mark: a three-colour wheel (红/黄/蓝) — the most literal way to say "this app
     is about colour". Vector, so no PNG densities are needed.

     GEOMETRY IS LOAD-BEARING, not decoration. An adaptive icon is a 108×108 canvas
     of which the launcher may show only the middle 66×66 circle (radius 33 around
     54,54). Draw outside it and the mask slices the mark — which is exactly what the
     first version shipped (top tick at y=5, colour chips down to y=82, nothing
     centred): "图标显示不全", reported 2026-09-28.

     LauncherIconTest asserts every element stays inside radius 33 of the centre and
     that the mark is centred, so this cannot regress silently.

     Geometry of the wheel, from the canvas centre (54,54):
       three 120° arcs on one circle of radius 25, stroke 9, butt caps
       → ring band r 20.5…29.5, so the whole mark reaches 29.5 (limit 33, margin 10%)
     The three arcs meet exactly at 30°, 150° and 270° (no gaps, no overlap), so the
     joints read as colour boundaries and nothing depends on draw order.
       red    −90° →  30°     #FF6B6B
       yellow  30° → 150°     #FFD166
       blue   150° → 270°     #4D96FF
     Any change here must be recomputed against the safe circle (and the test will
     insist on it: it derives each arc's circle from its endpoints + radius). -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- red: −90° → 30° -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M54,29 A25,25 0 0,1 75.651,66.5"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFF6B6B"
        android:strokeWidth="9" />

    <!-- yellow: 30° → 150° -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M75.651,66.5 A25,25 0 0,1 32.349,66.5"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFD166"
        android:strokeWidth="9" />

    <!-- blue: 150° → 270° -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32.349,66.5 A25,25 0 0,1 54,29"
        android:strokeColor="#FF4D96FF"
        android:strokeWidth="9" />
</vector>
